      "writtenOn": "2024-10-30T03:25:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, it actually will be stopped if the activity is destroyed.\nAppCompatActivity owns a LifeCycle. So when a AppCompatActivity is killed, the lifecycle launched coroutine is killed too.\n\nAnd we can run something when the lifecycle is destroyed with `finally` as the [doc](https://developer.android.com/topic/libraries/architecture/coroutines#suspend) shows. But I think this it\u0027s no need for this task? It\u0027s fine if the activity is killed before the maker file being deleted.\n\nI don\u0027t know any Kotlin experts. Or should I avoid using Kotlin? I may sometimes confuse others...\n\nI use Kotlin just because Java and Kotlin have the same familiarity to me. And Kotlin is more recommended.",
      "parentUuid": "f616b5a2_18f01f66",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "38971b158f7e76cf9ee92423714a376950620fc4",
